{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00084",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 7.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.75,
      "end_seconds": 12.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.12,
      "end_seconds": 16.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.5,
      "end_seconds": 20.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Alright, please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.45,
      "end_seconds": 25.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Um, so... a red eye. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.98,
      "end_seconds": 29.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.35,
      "end_seconds": 36.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "So, about... well, three days. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.83,
      "end_seconds": 39.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.86,
      "end_seconds": 47.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.07,
      "end_seconds": 53.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.41,
      "end_seconds": 55.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "I, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.01,
      "end_seconds": 61.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 61.3,
      "end_seconds": 66.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.67,
      "end_seconds": 68.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.11,
      "end_seconds": 72.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Have you had a sticky discharge in the morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.05,
      "end_seconds": 75.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Yeah. About four days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.7,
      "end_seconds": 79.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "So, did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.64,
      "end_seconds": 83.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.79,
      "end_seconds": 89.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Have you had any cold or pain in the eye?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.85,
      "end_seconds": 98.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "No, no cold, no pain in the eye. I did have a gritty feeling at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.5,
      "end_seconds": 106.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Any loss of vision, sensitivity to light or foreign body in the eye at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.62,
      "end_seconds": 114.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "I haven't had loss of vision, sensitivity to light or foreign body in the eye, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.9,
      "end_seconds": 117.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.03,
      "end_seconds": 119.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.37,
      "end_seconds": 122.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.94,
      "end_seconds": 128.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 128.99,
      "end_seconds": 135.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 71, temp 36.7 degrees, saturation 99 percent, pressure 111 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.69,
      "end_seconds": 139.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Okay, noted. What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.59,
      "end_seconds": 144.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "I had my appendix out about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.7,
      "end_seconds": 155.89,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.64,
      "end_seconds": 158.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.13,
      "end_seconds": 161.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Okay, does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.69,
      "end_seconds": 166.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "My sister has epilepsy. My father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.87,
      "end_seconds": 172.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "So, have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.74,
      "end_seconds": 185.46,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "For the most part, uh, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.68,
      "end_seconds": 190.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.69,
      "end_seconds": 203.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.65,
      "text": "I take hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. I've never really been one for hospitals. It's levetiracetam, 500 milligrams, twice a day for the seizures."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 204.16,
      "end_seconds": 210.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the levetiracetam was 1000 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.37,
      "end_seconds": 214.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.1,
      "end_seconds": 224.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed. I mean, I used to take Seretide inhaler, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.54,
      "end_seconds": 240.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.74,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.75,
      "end_seconds": 242.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.36,
      "end_seconds": 249.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.4,
      "end_seconds": 256.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "I mean, I have eczema, for five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.37,
      "end_seconds": 258.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.93,
      "end_seconds": 268.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "I've got epilepsy. I just want to get back to normal, you know, really. I've had asthma for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.03,
      "end_seconds": 276.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Go on. Right, so that's your known epilepsy. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.05,
      "end_seconds": 289.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.72,
      "end_seconds": 296.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.41,
      "end_seconds": 305.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, you know, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.03,
      "end_seconds": 309.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.89,
      "end_seconds": 310.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.25,
      "end_seconds": 321.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.86,
      "end_seconds": 324.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.05,
      "end_seconds": 326.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.58,
      "end_seconds": 330.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.41,
      "end_seconds": 353.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "The white of the eye is pink all over, and there's some sticky discharge on the lashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.83,
      "end_seconds": 356.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.08,
      "end_seconds": 374.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Your vision is normal on the chart and the pupil reacts well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.71,
      "end_seconds": 382.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Right, that's fine, you can get dressed. Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.56,
      "end_seconds": 388.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Yes, you know, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.3,
      "end_seconds": 401.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "Putting it all together, my working impression is conjunctivitis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep an allergic eye problem in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.58,
      "end_seconds": 406.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.05,
      "end_seconds": 423.29,
      "duration_seconds": 16.24,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like conjunctivitis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a red eye for three days, mild, and no loss of vision or cold."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.7,
      "end_seconds": 426.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.17,
      "end_seconds": 429.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.58,
      "end_seconds": 443.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Okay, that's done. I'm going to order an eye swab, for red eye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 444.23,
      "end_seconds": 445.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 446.71,
      "end_seconds": 469.15,
      "duration_seconds": 22.44,
      "text": "I'll start you on chloramphenicol eye drops, four times a day, for five days. That should help with conjunctivitis. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Wash your hands often, don't share towels, and don't rub the eye. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.71,
      "end_seconds": 480.89,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 482.21,
      "end_seconds": 483.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.34,
      "end_seconds": 492.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if your vision drops or the pain gets severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 494.01,
      "end_seconds": 495.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 496.22,
      "end_seconds": 498.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 499.06,
      "end_seconds": 500.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0076",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 501.51,
      "end_seconds": 505.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0077",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 506.82,
      "end_seconds": 514.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
